; pattern_miner_pure_mm2.mm2 — §9.3 of Notes on the Path to Scalable MeTTa Infrastructure
; (Ben Goertzel, 2025-06-30). Extracted verbatim via docs/specs/Mork/scalable_metta_infrastructure_spec.md §9.3.
;
; ─── WHY THIS IS VENDORED ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
; Our arrow-6 corpus is ARITHMETIC AND IDENTITY ONLY. This is the Hyperon greedy Pattern Miner, the
; same 7 stages, written by the person who defined the target — and it exercises precisely the
; classes our emitter DECLINES:
;   * multi-stage `exec` chaining with explicit `loc` staging (1..7) — our staging invariant
;   * threshold comparisons (here forced into exact-value matching, see stages 4 and 7)
;   * accumulators (stage 3 increments a count)
;
; ⚠️ READ §9.3.1 BEFORE TREATING A DECLINE HERE AS OUR DEFECT. Pure MM2 has NO built-in guards or
; arithmetic: "comparisons (>=,<) and arithmetic (+,-) can't be expressed directly; thresholds/counts
; need exhaustive rule enumeration or external primitives." That is why stages 4 and 7 below match an
; EXACT value (`?Minsup`, `?HighSurp`) instead of comparing — the paper's own workaround. The MM2+
; sibling (§9.2, pattern_miner_mm2plus.mm2) uses `:guard (>= ?N ?M)` for the same two stages, which is
; the exact difference to test.
;
; ⚠️ `loc` HERE IS A PLAIN INTEGER, "lower fires first" (§3.2). Our measured implementation orders by
; expression-preferring shortlex (d588832). The paper self-caveats as "a design sketch, not an
; implementation report", so OUR ordering is authoritative — do not "fix" toward this file.
;
; ⚠️ `(+ ?N 1)` in stage 3 and `(compute-I …)` in stage 6 are NOT pure-MM2 primitives; they are the
; paper's shorthand for the host-primitive layer (§8 `guard:<op>`). Ours is MORK's PURE_OPS. Stage 6's
; `compute-I` has no PURE_OPS equivalent at all. Expect declines here — record which, do not patch.
;
; allow-new-artifact: vendored upstream corpus; source spec read this session (§9.3)

; 1. Extract skeletons
(exec 1
  (, (eval (pred ?P) (list ?A1 ?A2)))
  (, (skeleton (eval (pred ?P) (list (var "$X") ?A2)))
     (skeleton (eval (pred ?P) (list ?A1 (var "$X"))))))

; 2. Instantiate candidates
(exec 2
  (, (skeleton ?Tpl)
     (eval (pred ?P) (list ?A1 ?A2)))
  (, (candidate (instantiate ?Tpl ?A1 ?A2))))

; 3. Increment support count
(exec 3
  (, (candidate ?C ?Pat)
     (count ?C ?Pat ?N))
  (, (count ?C ?Pat (+ ?N 1))))

; 4. Mark kept patterns when count equals minsup
(exec 4
  (, (count ?C ?Pat ?Minsup))
  (, (kept ?C ?Pat)))

; 5. Combine kept patterns into conjunctions
(exec 5
  (, (kept ?C1 ?P1)
     (kept ?C2 ?P2))
  (, (conj ?C1 ?C2 (and ?P1 ?P2))))

; 6. Compute surprisingness score
(exec 6
  (, (conj  ?C1 ?C2 ?And)
     (count ?C1 ?P1 ?N1)
     (count ?C2 ?P2 ?N2)
     (universe ?U))
  (, (score ?And (compute-I ?N1 ?N2 ?U))))

; 7. Select final outputs when score equals highsurp
(exec 7
  (, (score ?Pat ?I)
     (highsurp ?HighSurp))
  (, (output ?Pat ?I)))
